-- title:
--   Lemma 4.5 (orthogonal corners commute)
-- statement:
--   Let $E, F \in R$ be orthogonal idempotents ($EF = FE = 0$, $E^2 = E$), and suppose every pair of distinct indices has a third index outside it (automatic whenever $n \ge 3$). Then the subgroup $\mathrm{cornerSub}(E) \le \mathrm{St}_n(R)$ generated by roots with coefficients in $ERE$ commutes elementwise with the subgroup $\mathrm{cornerSub}(F)$ generated by roots with coefficients in $FRF$: $xy = yx$ for every $x \in \mathrm{cornerSub}(E)$, $y \in \mathrm{cornerSub}(F)$.
--
--   This is the preprint's Lemma 4.5, used together with Lemmas 4.3 and 4.4 in the four-corner splitting argument of Theorem 4.1's proof.
--
--   **Formalization Note** For two generators $x_{ij}(a)$, $x_{i'j'}(c)$ with $a \in ERE$, $c \in FRF$ (so $ac = ca = 0$), the generic case (index pairs sharing no common chain pattern) follows from the disjoint-commutator relation directly, one shared-index case follows from the chain-commutator relation collapsing via $ac=0$ or $ca=0$, and the case of exactly reversed pairs $x_{ij}(a)$, $x_{ji}(c)$ uses the preprint's own auxiliary-index trick (as in Lemma 4.3): writing $x_{ij}(a) = [x_{ik_0}(a), x_{k_0j}(E)]$ and showing $x_{ji}(c)$ commutes with each factor separately. The general statement then follows by a double induction on the generating closures. Zero `sorry` in the author's own proof, submitted separately.
-- source:
--   OpenAI, *Finite algebraic envelopes and the Boone-Higman conjecture*, OpenAI Math Release preprint, September 23, 2026, https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Finite-algebraic-envelopes-and-the-Boone-Higman-conjecture-September-23-2026/paper.pdf, Lemma 4.5, p. 13.

